sh_1.jpg"}},"ingredient/rice-hulls":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/rice-hulls","n":"Rice hulls","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Rice hulls or husks are the hard protecting coverings of grains of rice. In addition to protecting rice during the growing season, rice hulls can be put to use as building material, fertilizer, insulation material, or fuel. Rice hulls are part of the chaff of the rice."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-rice-hulls"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rice_hulls"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",[["Century egg","dish/century-egg"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Calcium oxide","ingredient/calcium-oxide"],["Clay","ingredient/clay"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Wood ash","ingredient/wood-ash"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/d/d6/Rice_chaffs.jpg/500px-Rice_chaffs.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"No machine-readable author provided. Green assumed (based on copyright claims).","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rice_chaffs.jpg"}},"ingredient/sport-peppers":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/sport-peppers","n":"Sport peppers","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Capsicum annuum is a flowering plant in the family Solanaceae (nightshades), native to the northern regions of South America and to southwestern North America. The plant produces berries of many colors including red, green, and yellow, often with pungent taste. It is one of the oldest cultivated crops, with domestication dating back to around 6,000 years ago in regions of Mexico. The genus Capsicum has over 30 species but Capsicum annuum is the primary species in its genus, as it has been widely cultivated for human consumption for a substantial amount of time and has spread across the world. This species has many uses in culinary and ornamental applications."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-sport-peppers"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sport_peppers"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Chicago-style hot dog","dish/chicago-style-hot-dog"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Celery salt","ingredient/celery-salt"],["Chicago-style relish","ingredient/chicago-style-relish"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Hot dog","ingredient/hot-dog"],["Kosher dill pickle","ingredient/kosher-dill-pickle"],["Mustard","ingredient/mustard"],["Mustard (condiment)","ingredient/mustard-condiment"],["Pickled cucumber","ingredient/pickled-cucumber"],["Poppy seed","ingredient/poppy-seed"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Vienna Beef","ingredient/vienna-beef"],["Vienna sausage","ingredient/vienna-sausage"],["White onion","ingredient/white-onion"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/d/d2/Capsicum_annuum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-027.jpg/500px-Capsicum_annuum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-027.jpg","w":500,"h":619,"by":"Franz Eugen Köhler, Köhler's Medizinal-Pflanzen","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Capsicum_annuum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-027.jpg"}},"dish/tandoori-roti":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/tandoori-roti","n":"Tandoori roti","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Tandoor bread is a flat bread baked in a clay oven called a tandoor. The technique has been in use for some five thousand years in Central and West Asia and the Indian subcontinent. It may be leavened or unleavened. It is often round, but may be made as elongated oval lavash or canoe-shaped shotis puri."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions